{
 "segments": [
  {
   "text": "Case Twenty-Four.",
   "start": 0.75,
   "end": 1.966,
   "pause": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "The Kite Festival.",
   "start": 2.566,
   "end": 3.803,
   "pause": 1.4
  },
  {
   "text": "Every year, Tidewhistle Cove holds a kite festival on the long beach. This year the weather was perfect. All day a steady breeze blew in from the sea toward the land. The flags on the harbour wall stood straight out, pointing inland toward the hills. Every kite on the beach leaned the same way, out over the dunes, and when little Rosie Hale let go of her balloon it sailed away over the village toward the hills.",
   "start": 5.203,
   "end": 29.545,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "The prize for the best kite was a wooden puffin, beautifully carved and painted, and it stood on a table in the judges' tent, down by the water's edge.",
   "start": 30.395,
   "end": 39.568,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "At four o'clock, while the judges were out on the sand admiring a kite shaped like a lobster, the wooden puffin disappeared.",
   "start": 40.418,
   "end": 47.885,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes Bell was one of the judges, and she asked around.",
   "start": 48.735,
   "end": 52.148,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Pip Carew had been flying his kite at the top of the beach, beside the dunes, with half his school class, and they all said he hadn't moved from that spot.",
   "start": 52.998,
   "end": 61.809,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Tamsin Trevelyan had been selling books at a stall by the car park all afternoon, with a queue that never seemed to get any shorter.",
   "start": 62.659,
   "end": 70.339,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Then there was Mr Penberthy, who had been seen hurrying away from the water's edge, near the judges' tent, at about four o'clock.",
   "start": 71.189,
   "end": 79.018,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Oh, I can explain that,\" said Mr Penberthy. \"My kite string snapped. The kite flew off out over the sea, so I ran down to the water's edge after it. Lost it, I'm afraid. It's probably halfway to France by now.\"",
   "start": 79.868,
   "end": 94.183,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes looked at the flags on the harbour wall. They were still pointing toward the hills.",
   "start": 95.033,
   "end": 99.662,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Can you solve it? What is wrong with Mr Penberthy's explanation?",
   "start": 100.762,
   "end": 104.602,
   "pause": 1.2
  },
  {
   "text": "Think about it.",
   "start": 105.802,
   "end": 106.826,
   "pause": 0.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Take a moment, or pause here if you are listening. When you are ready, the solution follows.",
   "start": 107.726,
   "end": 112.953,
   "pause": 4.5
  },
  {
   "text": "The Solution.",
   "start": 117.453,
   "end": 118.477,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Mr Penberthy took the wooden puffin.",
   "start": 119.577,
   "end": 121.966,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "All day the wind blew from the sea toward the land. The flags pointed inland, every kite leaned out over the dunes, and Rosie's balloon floated away over the village toward the hills. If Mr Penberthy's kite string really had snapped, his kite would have blown inland, over the dunes, not out to sea. He had no reason to run down to the water's edge, except to visit the judges' tent.",
   "start": 122.816,
   "end": 146.453,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Pip had been at the top of the beach with his whole class, and Tamsin had been busy at her book stall by the car park. Mr Penberthy was the one person seen near the tent, with a story that the wind proved untrue.",
   "start": 147.303,
   "end": 160.146,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "The wooden puffin was in his kite bag, along with his kite, which had never broken at all. He said he had come second at the festival five years running and simply wanted the puffin on his mantelpiece just once. He was asked to return it, and then, as a kindly joke, he was given a special prize for the most imaginative kite story of the day.",
   "start": 160.996,
   "end": 182.116,
   "pause": 0.0
  }
 ],
